    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0555" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/995</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hartman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-07T11:00:00-05:14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 7, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.05 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs has furnished this Legation copy of telegram
                    sent by him to the Minister for Foreign Affairs of Argentina dated December 5,
                    answering an invitation to Ecuador to attend Latin-American congress at Buenos
                    Aires next January to consider war. Telegram states that Ecuador accepts in
                    principle the assembly of an American congress that has for its purpose
                    solidarity of whole continent, and will be present if all American countries
                    previously reach a common agreement. The Minister for Foreign Affairs informed
                    me yesterday, orally, that Ecuador would attend Latin-American congress provided
                    plan was approved by the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
